# `spec/` is a specification a second implementation is checked against, and it is meant to be
# byte-identical on every machine that clones it. With `core.autocrlf=true` — which this repo is
# developed under — git would otherwise decide per file by sniffing its contents, so a schema
# checked out on Windows and the same schema on Linux hash differently. Nothing in the repo
# depends on that today (the freshness test reads through Python's universal newlines), but a
# port author comparing sha256s would have no way to tell a real difference from a checkout.
spec/** -text

# The gzipped vectors are already detected as binary by content. Stated anyway, because "already
# detected" is a property of the bytes and not a guarantee.
*.gz binary
